   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "UNET + text encoder: Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3 (or any repack \u2014 int8 convrot builds work too). Pair the Ref2VA PDD file with a ref2va UNET, FL2VA with fl2va.\n\nPDD Acc file goes in models/pdd_acc/ \u2014 either the original alibaba-pai/MiniMax-H3-Acc-LoRAs release or the pre-converted ComfyUI copy (aptech0081/MiniMax-H3-Acc-LoRAs-ComfyUI). Both load.\n\nOptional: wire reference images into ref_image_0... for identity-locked r2v."
   ],
   "title": "Models"
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1370,
    260
   ],
   "size": [
    270,
    300
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 18,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Sampler MUST be euler and sigmas MUST come from the Apply node / the PDD Acc Scheduler (trained PDD block boundaries). CFG 1.0 (BasicGuider). SigmaShift 12/3.\n\nBOTH passes run the same PDD model+guider; only the sigmas, noise and latent differ.\n\nNo turbo/distill LoRAs on top, no cache nodes (T8/EasyCache). Character LoRAs are fine."
   ],
   "title": "Recipe (do not change)"
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2030,
    260
   ],
   "size": [
    330,
    330
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 23,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Pass 1 renders 896x512; the latent upscale x1.5 lands exactly on the model-native 1344x768 \u2014 keep both ends inside the trained ~0.5-1MP range.\n\nScheduler denoise picks how much pass 2 repaints (it slices whole TRAINED blocks, so any value stays on the PDD grid):\n  0.125 -> 1 block  (resume sigma 0.632, subtle sharpen)\n  0.25  -> 2 blocks (resume sigma 0.8, default)\n  0.375 -> 3 blocks (resume sigma 0.878, strong repaint \u2014 composition can drift)\n\nAudio is decoded from PASS 1 (the refine pass re-noises its own audio copy only as joint-attention context; it is discarded), so the soundtrack is identical to the low-res render.\n\nThe nfe on the scheduler must match the Apply node (8)."
   ],
   "title": "Latent upscale knobs"
  }
 ],
